fix(sweep-policy): correct age-limit precedence and reject non-positive values (#3272)

Three fixes for worktree prune age-limit resolution:

1. parseDaemonBlock no longer materializes default 14/30 for absent
   maxAgeDaysClean/maxAgeDaysDirty keys — absent keys stay undefined
   so resolveSweepPolicy falls through to env vars and engine defaults.

2. worktree-prune-task.ts now uses resolveSweepPolicy instead of
   inlining parseInt(…) || 14/30, so all three call sites (CLI, REPL
   slash command, daemon task) share the same resolver.

3. resolveSweepPolicy rejects 0 and negative values at every layer
   via a positiveOrUndefined guard — AGE=0 would make every clean
   worktree immediately sweepable (data-loss risk).

Updated CliConfig type to make age fields optional. Added tests for
non-positive rejection (0, -5), absent-key passthrough in
parseDaemonBlock, and daemon task resolveSweepPolicy wiring.
